Subject: wined3d: use GDI present when the present-time client rect
 disagrees (issue 100)

The GL present path (0055) blits the backbuffer to the drawable and
y-flips through wined3d_texture_translate_drawable_coords(), which
queries the window's client rect on the CS thread at execution time.
The destination rect it flips was captured earlier, on the presenting
thread, in the window's DPI context (0023). Nothing guarantees the two
agree: the CS thread's DPI context can resolve the same window to a
different client height, and the window can be resized between capture
and execution. When they disagree the flip height no longer matches
the destination rect, and with GL's bottom-left origin the frame lands
low: a black band fills the top of the client area and the bottom rows
are clipped. Input hit-testing is unaffected, so clicks land on the
real layout, not the drawn one.

Reported twice with matching signatures: Live's frame about 476px low
on niri/XWayland at 125% (PR 98), and Live's UI sliding down under KDE
Plasma/NVIDIA when Live's 'Enable HiDPI Mode' setting is on (issue
100); that toggle changes Live's DPI awareness and resizes the window
after mapping.

Gate the fast path on agreement: re-query the client rect on the CS
thread right before the blit and compare it against the captured
destination rect. When they match, GL present proceeds as before; when
they do not, that frame takes swapchain_blit_gdi(), which anchors
top-left and presents the same frame correctly under the mismatch
(WINE_DISABLE_GL_PRESENT=1 renders correctly on the niri setup). On an
affected configuration every frame disagrees, so the swapchain stays
on the GDI path, behaving as if WINE_DISABLE_GL_PRESENT=1; healthy
configurations keep the GL path and its bandwidth win. The mismatch
branch routes to GDI explicitly rather than falling through: a
DISCARD-effect swapchain would otherwise reach the plain GL branch and
misplace the frame the same way.

A fire-once FIXME marks the first mismatched frame; a rate-limited
TRACE logs both rects and the backbuffer size, so an affected setup
records which side disagrees (DPI context vs in-flight resize) toward
a root fix in translate_drawable_coords itself.

Reports: v33 (Version33), PR 98; NoskyD, issue 100.
---
 dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c | 56 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c b/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
index d93ae04..0187087 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/swapchain.c
@@ -1280,6 +1280,34 @@ static bool swapchain_present_is_partial_copy(struct wined3d_swapchain *swapchai
     return false;
 }
 
+/* The GL present blit y-flips through wined3d_texture_translate_drawable_coords(),
+ * which queries the window's client rect on this (CS) thread at execution time.
+ * dst_rect was captured on the presenting thread in the window's DPI context
+ * (wined3d_swapchain_present).  When the two disagree - a DPI-awareness
+ * mismatch between the two threads, or a window resize since the capture -
+ * the flip height no longer matches the destination rect: GL's bottom-left
+ * origin then lands the frame low, black band on top, bottom rows clipped
+ * (issue 100; the niri report on PR 98).  The GDI present path anchors
+ * top-left and shows the same frame correctly under the mismatch. */
+static bool swapchain_gl_present_size_agrees(const struct wined3d_swapchain *swapchain, const RECT *dst_rect)
+{
+    static unsigned int mismatch_count;
+    RECT client_rect;
+
+    GetClientRect(swapchain->win_handle, &client_rect);
+    if (client_rect.right - client_rect.left == dst_rect->right - dst_rect->left
+            && client_rect.bottom - client_rect.top == dst_rect->bottom - dst_rect->top)
+        return true;
+
+    if (!mismatch_count++)
+        FIXME("Present-time client rect disagrees with the captured dst rect, using GDI present for these frames.\n");
+    if (mismatch_count <= 5 || !(mismatch_count % 300))
+        TRACE("Size disagreement #%u: dst %s, cs-thread client %s, backbuffer %ux%u.\n",
+                mismatch_count, wine_dbgstr_rect(dst_rect), wine_dbgstr_rect(&client_rect),
+                swapchain->state.desc.backbuffer_width, swapchain->state.desc.backbuffer_height);
+    return false;
+}
+
 static void swapchain_gl_present(struct wined3d_swapchain *swapchain,
         const RECT *src_rect, const RECT *dst_rect, unsigned int swap_interval, uint32_t flags)
 {
@@ -1312,17 +1340,27 @@ static void swapchain_gl_present(struct wined3d_swapchain *swapchain,
             && !(swapchain->state.desc.flags & WINED3D_SWAPCHAIN_FORCE_GDI_PRESENT)
             && context_gl->dc != wined3d_device_gl(swapchain->device)->backup_dc)
     {
-        static unsigned int gl_present_count;
-        gl_info = context_gl->gl_info;
+        if (swapchain_gl_present_size_agrees(swapchain, dst_rect))
+        {
+            static unsigned int gl_present_count;
+            gl_info = context_gl->gl_info;
 
-        if (!(gl_present_count++ % 60))
-            TRACE("GL popup present #%u: dc %p, win %p.\n",
-                    gl_present_count, context_gl->dc, swapchain->win_handle);
+            if (!(gl_present_count++ % 60))
+                TRACE("GL popup present #%u: dc %p, win %p.\n",
+                        gl_present_count, context_gl->dc, swapchain->win_handle);
 
-        swapchain_gl_set_swap_interval(swapchain, context_gl, swap_interval);
-        wined3d_texture_load_location(back_buffer, 0, context, back_buffer->resource.draw_binding);
-        swapchain_blit(swapchain, context, src_rect, dst_rect);
-        gl_info->gl_ops.wgl.p_wglSwapBuffers(context_gl->dc);
+            swapchain_gl_set_swap_interval(swapchain, context_gl, swap_interval);
+            wined3d_texture_load_location(back_buffer, 0, context, back_buffer->resource.draw_binding);
+            swapchain_blit(swapchain, context, src_rect, dst_rect);
+            gl_info->gl_ops.wgl.p_wglSwapBuffers(context_gl->dc);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            /* Not the fall-through chain below: a DISCARD-effect swapchain
+             * would otherwise reach the plain GL branch and misplace the
+             * frame the same way. */
+            swapchain_blit_gdi(swapchain, context, src_rect, dst_rect);
+        }
     }
     else if (context_gl->dc == wined3d_device_gl(swapchain->device)->backup_dc
             || (swapchain->state.desc.flags & WINED3D_SWAPCHAIN_FORCE_GDI_PRESENT)
